{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2189-10-15 02:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good evening. I'm Dr. Lee, one of the surgical team. You're here because of abdominal pain and not passing gas. Can you tell me more about what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2189-10-15 02:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, the pain started about 12 hours ago. It feels like my old blockages. I haven’t passed flatus since this morning. I’ve been having these episodes for years because of my sclerosing mesenteritis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2189-10-15 02:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And you mentioned forgetfulness yesterday—has that improved?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2189-10-15 02:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s gone now. It scared me, but it only lasted a few hours."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2189-10-15 02:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, good. We reviewed your CT scans from earlier today. There’s no sign of a complete bowel obstruction, but your G-tube appears blocked. We’ll place an NG tube temporarily to help decompress your stomach."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2189-10-15 02:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will that hurt? I’ve had NG tubes before—they’re uncomfortable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2189-10-15 02:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It can be uncomfortable, but we’ll guide it gently through your nose. We’ll also give you something to help with the discomfort. It’s temporary—just until we fix the G-tube issue."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2189-10-15 02:45:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I trust you. What about my G-tube? It’s been acting up since I stopped venting it at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2189-10-15 02:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s likely why it’s clogged. Thick mucus built up. We’ll clean it out and may need to replace and upsize it so it doesn’t happen again. That’s planned for later in the week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2189-10-15 02:50:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had so many surgeries… I just want this managed without another big operation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2189-10-15 02:52:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re not planning surgery. This is a minor procedure with radiology. You’ll be sedated, and they’ll replace the tube using imaging to guide it. Very low risk."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2189-10-15 02:55:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That sounds better. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2189-10-15 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How are you feeling? The NG tube is working—your stomach is decompressing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2189-10-15 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "The pain is a bit better, but I hate this tube. When can we remove it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2189-10-15 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Once your G-tube is replaced and working well. We’re scheduling that for Thursday. In the meantime, we’re keeping you NPO—no food or drink by mouth."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2189-10-15 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No food? How will I get nutrition?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2189-10-15 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll give you IV fluids and electrolytes. Since you’re off TPN now, we’re not restarting it unless needed. Your body just needs a rest right now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2189-10-15 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my other meds? I take gabapentin, lamotrigine, and aripiprazole."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2189-10-15 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve restarted those. You’re getting them through the IV or crushed, since you can’t swallow pills right now. We’re monitoring for any side effects."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2189-10-15 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs came back. Your white count is normal, no sign of infection. But your hemoglobin is low—9.2—and your bicarbonate is a bit low, suggesting mild metabolic acidosis. We’ll keep an eye on it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2189-10-15 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that serious? I’ve always been anemic."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2189-10-15 14:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s consistent with your history of chronic disease. We’re not transfusing—you’re stable. But we’ll make sure you’re getting enough iron and nutrients when you start eating again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2189-10-16 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "How’s the pain today? Still managing okay with the Dilaudid?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2189-10-16 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, the pain is much better. I don’t need it as often. Can I try sipping water?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2189-10-16 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not yet. We want to wait until after your G-tube is replaced. We don’t want to risk worsening the obstruction."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2189-10-16 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. I just miss normal routines."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2189-10-17 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—your G-tube replacement is scheduled for tomorrow morning. The radiology team will upsize it to reduce future clogs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2189-10-17 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m a little nervous. Will I be awake?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2189-10-17 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll get light sedation—fentanyl and midazolam—so you’ll be relaxed and won’t feel pain. Someone will monitor your vitals the whole time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2189-10-17 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that helps. And after? When can I eat?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2189-10-17 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll start with a liquid diet the next day if all goes well. We’ll also begin a new medication called methylnaltrexone to help with bowel motility."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2189-10-17 10:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What does that do?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2189-10-17 10:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It helps stimulate your bowels without affecting pain control. It’s especially useful for people on narcotics who have slow motility."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2189-10-18 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, you just came back from the procedure. It went perfectly. Your G-tube was upsized to 16 French and is working well. You tolerated sedation without issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2189-10-18 12:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel groggy, but okay. Is the old tube gone?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2189-10-18 12:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, replaced and confirmed in the right spot with imaging. We’ll remove the NG tube later today once we see the G-tube is venting properly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2189-10-18 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The G-tube is draining well. We’ve removed the NG tube. You can start small sips of water now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2189-10-18 15:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you! That’s a relief. Can I have broth tomorrow?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2189-10-18 15:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If you tolerate water, we’ll advance to clear liquids tomorrow. We’re making good progress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2189-10-19 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. We got your urine culture back—it shows Klebsiella pneumoniae, but you’re not running a fever or having symptoms. We don’t think you need antibiotics."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2189-10-19 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that a UTI? I’ve had those before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2189-10-19 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly, but since you’re not symptomatic, we’ll just monitor. Treating it without symptoms could lead to resistance. We’ll check again if you develop fever or pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2189-10-19 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2189-10-20 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re now on full liquids and your bowels are moving. We’re going to switch your pain meds to Dilaudid suppositories as needed. You said you have some at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2189-10-20 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I have a few left. I’ll use them sparingly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2189-10-20 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We’re also sending you home on methylnaltrexone to keep your motility improved. And ranitidine for reflux."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2189-10-20 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need another follow-up with GI?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2189-10-20 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, in two weeks with Dr. Evans. They’ll assess your G-tube care and overall bowel function. We want to prevent future blockages."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2189-10-21 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done great. We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow. You’re tolerating food, pain is minimal, and your G-tube is working."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2189-10-21 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m ready to go home. What should I watch for?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2189-10-21 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call us if you have severe pain, can’t pass gas, or develop a fever over 101. Also, make sure to vent your G-tube regularly to avoid mucus buildup."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2189-10-21 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my meds? I take a lot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2189-10-21 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll continue all your home meds: gabapentin, lamotrigine, aripiprazole, and the new ones—ranitidine and methylnaltrexone. We’re not giving a new Dilaudid script since you have suppositories at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2189-10-21 09:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about driving?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2189-10-21 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not until you’re off pain meds. Even then, go slow. You might feel weak or tired for a few weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2189-10-21 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The physical therapist saw you today. You’re strong enough to go home with visiting nursing services to help with G-tube care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2189-10-21 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. I was worried about managing alone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2189-10-22 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your discharge orders are ready. You’re going home today. We’ll review everything with you before you leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2189-10-22 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you so much. I feel much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2189-10-22 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Remember: vent your G-tube daily, take your meds, and follow up in two weeks. Call us if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2189-10-22 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I’ve learned my lesson—no skipping G-tube care!"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2189-10-22 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. That’s the best way to avoid another hospital stay. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2189-10-22 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2189-10-22 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will be in with your discharge paperwork and prescriptions shortly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2189-10-22 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. I’m ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2189-10-22 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing—your urine culture showed Klebsiella, but since you’re not symptomatic, no treatment is needed. Just monitor for burning or urgency."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2189-10-22 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. I’ll keep an eye on it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2189-10-22 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And if you have migraines or asthma flares, use your usual rescue meds. You’re cleared for light activity, but avoid heavy lifting for six weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2189-10-22 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll take it easy. Thank you for explaining everything so clearly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2189-10-22 08:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re very welcome. We’re glad you’re feeling better. Have a safe trip home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 71,
      "time": "2189-10-22 08:27:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I appreciate all the care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 72,
      "time": "2189-10-22 08:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care of yourself. Call us with any concerns."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 73,
      "time": "2189-10-22 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Goodbye for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 74,
      "time": "2189-10-22 08:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Goodbye."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 75,
      "time": "2189-10-22 08:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "See you at follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 76,
      "time": "2189-10-22 08:37:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Looking forward to it. Rest well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 77,
      "time": "2189-10-22 08:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 78,
      "time": "2189-10-22 08:41:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will assist you with discharge soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 79,
      "time": "2189-10-22 08:43:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’m ready when they are."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 80,
      "time": "2189-10-22 08:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Have a smooth recovery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 81,
      "time": "2189-10-22 08:47:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 82,
      "time": "2189-10-22 08:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 83,
      "time": "2189-10-22 08:51:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Bye."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 84,
      "time": "2189-10-22 08:53:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Goodbye."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 85,
      "time": "2189-10-22 08:55:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "See you soon."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2189-10-15 02:31:00",
    "admission_end": "2189-10-22 16:00:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of sclerosing mesenteritis and chronic intestinal dysmotility was admitted for acute abdominal pain and failure to pass flatus, consistent with a transient small bowel obstruction. She was found to have a blocked G-tube, which was contributing to her symptoms. An NG tube was placed for decompression, and the G-tube was successfully upsized via interventional radiology. Her pain was well-controlled with Dilaudid, and she was started on methylnaltrexone to improve bowel motility. A urine culture grew Klebsiella pneumoniae, but she remained asymptomatic and did not require antibiotics. She advanced to a regular diet, was stable, and discharged home with nursing support and follow-up plans. Key instructions included regular G-tube venting, medication adherence, and monitoring for signs of obstruction or infection.",
    "problems": [
      "Unspecified intestinal obstruction",
      "Other mechanical complication of other gastrointestinal prosthetic devices, implants and grafts, initial encounter",
      "Urinary tract infection, site not specified",
      "Dehydration",
      "Functional dyspepsia",
      "Gastro-esophageal reflux disease without esophagitis",
      "Unspecified asthma, uncomplicated",
      "Migraine, unspecified, not intractable, without status migrainosus",
      "Long term (current) use of anticoagulants",
      "Personal history of transient ischemic attack (TIA), and cerebral infarction without residual deficits",
      "Personal history of other venous thrombosis and embolism"
    ]
  }
}
